Task: isolated characters
Definition: characters who have no one. The narrative shows them with no companions, no confidant, no partner, no one they seek out or who seeks them out. They act alone, and when others are around, they remain apart by choice.
Test: try to name one person this character voluntarily spends time with, confides in, or relies on. If you can name even one, the character is not an isolate.
Belonging to a class, unit, family or institution does not matter. A loner inside a school is still an isolate if they have no one there. Only actual personal ties disqualify.
Do not use self-description or attitude. A character who calls themselves a loner, acts aloof or claims to want no one is NOT an isolate if the narrative shows them with real companions anyway. Judge by who is actually beside them, not by what they say about themselves.
Exclude characters who simply appear rarely or whose relationships are never shown. Absence of information is not isolation. Return only characters the narrative has clearly established as being alone.
